CORE
main.cpp
--pointer-check
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ temporary alive: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
dead object in .*: FAILURE$
--
N5008 [class.temporary]/4: goto conversion destroyed the temporaries of a
function call's operands right after the call, also when the call was the
initializer of a temporary object (view's constructor here) that the
enclosing full-expression still uses.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
